From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:07:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/34] surface lazy: an attachment read copies the image, not
 the bytes

On Sim, every 1206x2622 surface has one guest texture. The second image beside
each is the attachment read's usage shadow: a draw samples at its own pixel the
surface its pass renders. That shadow's truth was the bytes, with a Lazy of its
own, so the attachment copied back before each read (not alone in its encoder),
beside_another refused the rest, and the shadow copied in again.

For a lazy surface, whose image holds every usage, the shadow's truth is now
that image. The encoder brings the image current first, inside what the copy
reads, also for a clear or a pass that names only the copy; a copy into the
image leaves the copy behind, and it goes to no later encoder, whose byte writes
it could not see.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
